# UI/UX designer — alpine booking portal

The public site is a light international adventure desk: white and off-white surfaces, deep black type, and one fresh alpine green for action. Do not use black or charcoal as a section background or as a card fill. Photography may lead a hero or a card, and the reading copy sits on white beneath it. Do not invent open dates, prices, phone numbers, or a rescue line.

## Tokens

Defined in `app/globals.css` under `@theme`:

- `canvas` page ground `#f4f6f4`, `paper` cards `#ffffff`
- `ink` headings and body `#1a1d1b`, `muted` secondary text `#5c6560`, `line` borders `#e3e7e3`
- `alpine` / `alpine-deep` primary buttons, badges, and active nav. White text on the green fill.
- `alpine-soft` secondary badges
- `danger` warnings `#9d2c2c`

The root font size is 16px and body copy is 1rem with relaxed line height. Headings use `font-display`, bold weight, and tight tracking.

## Type and layout

- `Manrope` for titles. `Source Sans 3` for body, forms, and legal lines.
- Hero and page titles are `text-4xl` on small screens and `text-5xl` at most on desktop. Section titles are `text-3xl` to `text-4xl`. Card titles are `text-xl` to `text-2xl`.
- Body copy is `text-base` with `leading-relaxed`. Secondary details, eyebrows, and table labels are `text-sm`.
- Buttons are `min-h-11`, `text-base`, medium weight, and sentence case.
- Generous page padding. Cards are white, `rounded-3xl`, lightly bordered, and use a soft shadow. Hover lifts the card.
- Sticky white header. The current section is alpine green.
- A homepage hero may show a full-width photograph. The title, search, and actions sit on a white panel over the lower edge of the photo.
- Itinerary is a vertical list a phone can scan, with large day titles. Departure rows show date, seats or bike slots, INR price, and a status badge.
- SUV and motorbike stay labeled differently.

## Interaction

- Primary button is alpine, sentence-case: "Request to book" or "Request a quote".
- Expedition cards may zoom the photograph on hover and rise slightly. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- "Limited slots" and "Extreme altitude" badges only when seats or the difficulty field say so.
- Open departures use a green badge. Full batches use a charcoal badge and stay visible, not bookable.
- Sticky mobile bar on expedition pages: price and the primary action, on white.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Focus rings stay visible on white.
- Forms use large inputs, visible labels, and helper text for permit and fitness questions.

## Content tone

Direct and calm. "Day 4 — Tanglang La, 5,328 m. Long riding day; support vehicle in convoy." Do not promise open passes.
